1
00:00:01,292 --> 00:00:05,384
Hi, we're team SCE3-04 from SC2006.

2
00:00:05,555 --> 00:00:09,364
This is PlugPlan SG, a web app that helps electric-vehicle

3
00:00:09,384 --> 00:00:12,082
drivers in Singapore decide where to charge,

4
00:00:12,332 --> 00:00:14,733
how much to charge, and what it will cost,

5
00:00:14,753 --> 00:00:16,200
before they set off.

6
00:00:18,625 --> 00:00:21,612
Charger maps already tell you where a charger is.

7
00:00:21,770 --> 00:00:24,184
What they don't tell you is whether you can reach it,

8
00:00:24,204 --> 00:00:27,026
whether the plug fits your car, how long you'd wait,

9
00:00:27,046 --> 00:00:28,889
and whether it's worth the detour.

10
00:00:29,060 --> 00:00:32,540
PlugPlan combines live charger data from LTA DataMall with

11
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:35,652
OneMap routing, and turns it into a short,

12
00:00:35,810 --> 00:00:39,375
explained list of charging stops for one specific trip.

13
00:00:41,616 --> 00:00:43,339
Let's start as a driver.

14
00:00:43,497 --> 00:00:46,609
If the password is wrong, the error is deliberately generic,

15
00:00:46,629 --> 00:00:49,405
so it never reveals whether an account exists.

16
00:00:50,942 --> 00:00:53,824
Sign-in is handled by Supabase Auth.

17
00:00:53,995 --> 00:00:56,508
There are two roles, Driver and Moderator,

18
00:00:56,732 --> 00:00:59,205
and every permission is checked on the server.

19
00:01:00,716 --> 00:01:02,611
First, the vehicle profile.

20
00:01:02,782 --> 00:01:06,748
Battery capacity, energy consumption, compatible plugs,

21
00:01:06,768 --> 00:01:10,939
and maximum AC and DC power all feed into the calculation.

22
00:01:11,111 --> 00:01:14,143
The twenty percent reserve means every plan keeps at least

23
00:01:14,163 --> 00:01:16,782
twenty percent of battery when you arrive.

24
00:01:18,809 --> 00:01:22,453
Now a real trip: from NTU to Marina Bay Sands,

25
00:01:22,677 --> 00:01:26,026
starting with only eighteen percent battery and up to an hour

26
00:01:26,046 --> 00:01:30,328
to charge. Place search uses OneMap, so the driver picks an

27
00:01:30,348 --> 00:01:33,467
exact location instead of typing free text.

28
00:01:35,009 --> 00:01:38,476
When I click Find charging options, the server asks OneMap

29
00:01:38,496 --> 00:01:42,055
for routes and LTA DataMall for charger locations and live

30
00:01:42,075 --> 00:01:45,857
connector status. Each result shows its data source and when

31
00:01:45,877 --> 00:01:48,686
it was retrieved. Notice the target:

32
00:01:48,706 --> 00:01:51,535
we don't tell you to charge to a hundred percent.

33
00:01:51,706 --> 00:01:54,778
We calculate just enough to reach the destination with the

34
00:01:54,798 --> 00:01:59,153
reserve intact. Every card shows the estimated charging time,

35
00:01:59,351 --> 00:02:02,548
cost, detour, and why it was recommended.

36
00:02:05,762 --> 00:02:08,052
The assumptions are always visible.

37
00:02:08,236 --> 00:02:11,098
And at the bottom, you can see which stations were excluded,

38
00:02:11,118 --> 00:02:14,374
and why: an incompatible plug, too long a detour,

39
00:02:14,394 --> 00:02:16,275
or no free connector right now.

40
00:02:17,809 --> 00:02:21,105
Compare options puts every candidate side by side on the same

41
00:02:21,125 --> 00:02:26,144
metrics: cost, charging time, detour, arrival battery,

42
00:02:26,164 --> 00:02:29,960
and overall score. Each option trades time against cost in

43
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:31,111
a different way.

44
00:02:34,342 --> 00:02:36,263
I'll select the top-ranked one.

45
00:02:36,394 --> 00:02:38,855
Selecting a stop saves a preference.

46
00:02:39,026 --> 00:02:42,585
It isn't a booking, because PlugPlan does not reserve chargers

47
00:02:42,605 --> 00:02:43,921
or take payments.

48
00:02:45,475 --> 00:02:48,548
With one click, the plan opens in Google Maps,

49
00:02:48,568 --> 00:02:51,068
with the charging stop already on the route.

50
00:02:53,175 --> 00:02:57,090
Priorities change. Switching the strategy to Fastest journey

51
00:02:57,110 --> 00:03:00,899
recalculates the ranking and saves a new plan version.

52
00:03:02,409 --> 00:03:05,560
Older versions are kept read-only, with their original inputs

53
00:03:05,580 --> 00:03:08,678
and results, so you can always see what was recommended,

54
00:03:08,698 --> 00:03:12,455
and why. When the server reuses route data from the last ten

55
00:03:12,475 --> 00:03:16,948
minutes, the result is labelled Cached, with its real timestamps.

56
00:03:19,175 --> 00:03:21,320
Live data isn't always right.

57
00:03:21,491 --> 00:03:24,695
If a driver finds a faulty charger, they can report it with

58
00:03:24,715 --> 00:03:27,202
a short description and an optional photo:

59
00:03:27,570 --> 00:03:31,794
JPEG, PNG or WebP, up to five megabytes.

60
00:03:33,342 --> 00:03:35,276
The report starts as Pending.

61
00:03:35,447 --> 00:03:38,803
A single unreviewed report never removes a station.

62
00:03:38,947 --> 00:03:41,500
A moderator has to review it first.

63
00:03:43,029 --> 00:03:46,371
Now, in a separate window, we're signed in as a moderator.

64
00:03:46,542 --> 00:03:49,838
The review screen puts the driver's evidence next to LTA's

65
00:03:49,858 --> 00:03:52,108
official status for that connector.

66
00:03:55,309 --> 00:03:58,118
Every decision, whether it's verify, reject,

67
00:03:58,138 --> 00:04:01,105
merge, resolve, or expire, needs a reason,

68
00:04:01,125 --> 00:04:03,256
and it's written to an audit history.

69
00:04:03,440 --> 00:04:06,559
If two moderators act on the same report at once,

70
00:04:06,625 --> 00:04:09,986
the second one gets a conflict instead of silently overwriting

71
00:04:10,006 --> 00:04:11,006
the first.

72
00:04:13,375 --> 00:04:17,079
Back to the driver. Refreshing the saved plan fetches live

73
00:04:17,099 --> 00:04:18,152
data again.

74
00:04:19,409 --> 00:04:22,343
The verified faulty station is now filtered out,

75
00:04:22,580 --> 00:04:26,283
the old selection is cleared, and PlugPlan suggests the next

76
00:04:26,303 --> 00:04:30,146
best alternative. But the driver makes the final choice.

77
00:04:30,317 --> 00:04:33,783
Nothing is switched automatically, and earlier versions stay

78
00:04:33,803 --> 00:04:34,843
untouched.

79
00:04:38,625 --> 00:04:42,954
Under the hood, PlugPlan is built with Next.js and TypeScript.

80
00:04:43,125 --> 00:04:47,000
Supabase provides authentication, a Postgres database with

81
00:04:47,020 --> 00:04:50,362
row-level security, and private image storage,

82
00:04:50,599 --> 00:04:53,849
and the app is deployed on Vercel in the Singapore region.

83
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:57,092
The ranking engine is hand-written and covered by unit tests

84
00:04:57,112 --> 00:05:01,224
with fixed numerical expectations, plus eight end-to-end browser

85
00:05:01,244 --> 00:05:05,099
journeys. In a load test of a hundred concurrent requests,

86
00:05:05,296 --> 00:05:08,415
ninety-five percent finished in under two seconds.

87
00:05:11,446 --> 00:05:15,926
PlugPlan SG. Charge enough, not full, with every recommendation

88
00:05:15,946 --> 00:05:18,459
explained. Thanks for watching.

